{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/767151-disciplines-do-you-know","id":767151,"title":"Disciplines! Do you know?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T10:49:11-08:00","id":767151,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Disciplines! Do you know?","content":"Do you know when they work or fail? How do you know? <br /> <br /> When you have majesty and you summon someone, They get the uncontrollable urge to come to you, but do you know that they are coming? Do you know if you &quot;connected with them&quot;? What if you tried to summon someone who was dead or in torpor?<br /> <br /> If I dominate someone and tell them to do something for me, do I know they are dominated? What if they know what I tried to do and are just playing the part in order to stab me in the back later?<br /> <br /> Or 2nd dot of Majesty.. the list could go on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:26:58-08:00","id":767171,"title":"","content":"I generally let the players believe what they want unless it's obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T14:59:09-08:00","id":767358,"title":"","content":"I would say reveal it just like a skill roll failure. As long as they can observe the outcome they can be aware of how it resolved. You do not know if you have convinced someone to do something or even just to believe your lie until you observe their reaction. The questions you must ask is:<br /> a) is the failure expressed on the individual notably, would a successful domination change their expression, body language etc that the lack of would make the failure observable?<br /> b) since the vampire is using a supernatural power are they aware of it after they use it, is it a fire and forget or a matter of finesse? The reason this is important is because if it is a fire and forget like ability then I would say they must be able to observe the failure to know but if it is something that they actively work to do they may be able to notice that they were unable to progress to the next step.<br /> <br /> I do not believe it is directly stated that a player is aware of their failures and successes automatically but I do believe that the spirit of the game is that the st will inform the player when it is relevant, which in most cases is as the failure occurs but not always.<br /> <br /> Example scene where failure not being directly stated can add to the story:<br /> <br /> Pc wants a password from someone. They use their power or skill set to try and extract the desired information [failure on power or skill]<br /> Npc understands what will happen (possibly violence) if they do not comply so they try to give a fake password [Success on Contested subterfuge skill roll]<br /> Pc believes they have the correct password since they believed the lie and act on this perception.<br /> <br /> The problem arises with meta-gaming since there will be times where a player is aware they (should have) failed and potentially act on this out of character information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:54:58-08:00","id":767509,"title":"","content":"Dominate is not an obvious power, you don't know if it worked in the same way your victim and observers don't know you were using the Discipline at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T01:06:21-08:00","id":767642,"title":"","content":"The book says that in the event of a failed use of a discipline some random spooky thing happens in the near vicinity. Like lights flickering or it suddenly getting a bit colder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T20:09:12-08:00","id":768252,"title":"","content":"Alright. So dominate or Majesty they could bluff you into thinking you charmed/mezmerized them, but how about summoning someone? Do you know if they are actually coming to you? What if you tried to summon someone who was dead or in torpor? What would the character feel? Obviously the power would fail, but would they sit around and wait for the person to show up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:50:24-08:00","id":774909,"title":"","content":"I'd say they couldn't tell: if the person doesn't show up, is it because of death or because she's being held captive ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}